# Running local Odoo

Start, stop, logs:

```bash
docker compose up -d
docker compose stop
docker compose logs -f odoo
```

- Web UI: http://localhost:8069
- Database manager: http://localhost:8069/web/database/manager
- Local database name: `hp`. Create it without demo data.
- Master password is the Odoo default `admin`. It is local only.

Update the image within Odoo 20 (new nightly build):

```bash
docker compose pull && docker compose up -d
```

Install or upgrade custom modules, then restart Odoo:

```bash
docker compose run --rm odoo odoo -d hp -i hp_module --stop-after-init
docker compose run --rm odoo odoo -d hp -u hp_module --stop-after-init
docker compose restart odoo
```

- Use `-i` the first time a module is installed, `-u` after changing XML views, data files, or models.
- Python changes reload automatically in dev mode, but restart after install or upgrade.
- Do not run a local Odoo from source or a Python venv.
- Do not run `docker compose down -v` unless the user asks for a clean reset. It deletes all local data.
